{
  "category": "Kite Pokémon",
  "entries": [
    {
      "text": "A friendly Pokémon that captures the subtle flows of seawater using its two antennae.",
      "version": "diamond"
    },
    {
      "text": "Scientists discovered that the distinctive patterns on its back differ by region.",
      "version": "pearl"
    },
    {
      "text": "People organize tours to see this Pokémon frolic and skim the tops of waves with REMORAID.",
      "version": "platinum"
    },
    {
      "text": "When it swims close to the surface of the ocean, people aboard ships are able to observe the pattern on its back.",
      "version": "heartgold"
    },
    {
      "text": "When it swims close to the surface of the ocean, people aboard ships are able to observe the pattern on its back.",
      "version": "soulsilver"
    },
    {
      "text": "People organize tours to see this Pokémon frolic and skim the tops of waves with Remoraid.",
      "version": "black"
    },
    {
      "text": "People organize tours to see this Pokémon frolic and skim the tops of waves with Remoraid.",
      "version": "white"
    },
    {
      "text": "The pattern on its back varies by region. It often swims in a school of Remoraid.",
      "version": "black-2"
    },
    {
      "text": "The pattern on its back varies by region. It often swims in a school of Remoraid.",
      "version": "white-2"
    },
    {
      "text": "The pattern on its back varies by region. It often swims in a school of Remoraid.",
      "version": "x"
    },
    {
      "text": "When it swims close to the surface of the ocean, people aboard ships are able to observe the pattern on its back.",
      "version": "y"
    },
    {
      "text": "The pattern on its back varies by region. It often swims in a school of Remoraid.",
      "version": "omega-ruby"
    },
    {
      "text": "When it swims close to the surface of the ocean, people aboard ships are able to observe the pattern on its back.",
      "version": "alpha-sapphire"
    },
    {
      "text": "It’s highly friendly and easily tamed. Tours that take people swimming with Mantyke are a super-popular beach activity.",
      "version": "ultra-sun"
    },
    {
      "text": "Mantyke are friendly toward people and will approach boats closely. The patterns on their backs differ depending on their habitat.",
      "version": "ultra-moon"
    },
    {
      "text": "Mantyke living in Galar seem to be somewhat sluggish. The colder waters of the seas in this region may be the cause.",
      "version": "sword"
    },
    {
      "text": "It swims along with a school of Remoraid, and they’ll all fight together to repel attackers.",
      "version": "shield"
    },
    {
      "text": "Though ball-like in shape, this Pokémon is a proficient swimmer. I have discovered that if a Mantyke spends much time with schools of Remoraid, it will eventually achieve evolution.",
      "version": "legends-arceus"
    }
  ],
